{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs2h1Y38s8huP9h4cDeB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `fetcher` package is now async, and all 8 tests pass (`python3 -m pytest -q`, 0.23s). I haven't committed anything.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`fetcher/client.py`**: `Client(transport=None, retries=3, backoff=0.01, max_concurrency=5)`. `get` is async with retries that use `asyncio.sleep` and only catch `TransientError`. `get_many` uses a semaphore and `asyncio.gather`, so results keep input order and per-URL errors come back as `FetchError` instances. `close()` is async, and `async with` is supported. The default transport is async and uses `asyncio.sleep(0.01)`.\n- **`fetcher/aggregate.py`**: `summarize` is async and returns the same dict shape.\n- **`fetcher/sync.py`** (new): `fetch_all(urls, transport=None)` runs `Client.get_many` under `asyncio.run`. I also exported `sync` from `fetcher/__init__.py` to match `aggregate`.\n- **`tests/test_client.py`**: ported to plain `asyncio.run`, so there's no new dependency. I kept the original three tests and added five: non-transient errors aren't retried, results keep order while concurrency stays within the limit, `get_many` actually runs concurrently, a closed client raises, and `fetch_all` works.\n\n**Choices you may want to change**\n\n- Tests use `asyncio.run` rather than pytest-asyncio.\n- `max_concurrency` bounds the whole `get`, including its retries and backoff sleeps. A retrying URL keeps its slot while it waits.\n- `get_many` still wraps any exception in `FetchError`, as the sync version did, so only `TransientError` is retried and everything else is reported per URL."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1179,"cache_read_input_tokens":44365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1179},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b4b773a-e876-45f4-9f4a-4ab20faa7d46","uuid":"6eccaa58-efce-4bc8-9a87-646379b2b821","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:07:20.638Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs2h1CwkVUe3Ue63ZJ8M"}
